  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10c-catfishes-remaining-catfish-from-south-america/ageneiosus_cf_atronasus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Reaches only about 12 cm in total length. Origin: Peru. Available size: 5–6 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10c-catfishes-remaining-catfish-from-south-america/ageneiosus_cf_atronasus_en/",
      "html": "<p>This interesting dolphin catfish was imported from Peru for the first time. In contrast to many of its congeners, this species stays relatively small and reaches only 12 cm in total length, so it is also suitable for normally sized home aquaria. Keep in mind, however, that these catfishes are predatory and tankmates must not be too small. Otherwise the dolphin cat is a peaceful species.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10c-catfishes-remaining-catfish-from-south-america/ageneiosus_cf_atronasus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Predatory, but otherwise peaceful.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10c-catfishes-remaining-catfish-from-south-america/ageneiosus_cf_atronasus_en/",
      "html": "<p>During the breeding season the males develop very long dorsal spines.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10c-catfishes-remaining-catfish-from-south-america/ageneiosus_cf_atronasus_en/",
      "html": "<p>During breeding season the males develop very long dorsal spines that are used during mating to hold the female. Insemination is internal, but most details of the natural history of these fishes are still unknown.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10c-catfishes-remaining-catfish-from-south-america/ageneiosus_cf_atronasus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Ageneiosus: from ancient Greek, meaning \"without a beard\"; this refers to the fact that the barbels are usually hidden and cannot be seen externally. atronasus: Latin, meaning \"with a black nose\".</p>"
    }
  ],
